  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Support to Civil Society in Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The European Union backs civil society actors in promoting democracy and reducing social tensions. Despite restrictions on their operations, the EU has actively supported civil society organizations (CSOs) in Bangladesh. This includes grant awards and a governance programme (Platforms for Dialogue) that empowered CSOs to engage with citizens and the government, strengthening governance at local and national levels.In alignment with the EU&apos;s efforts, the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) has initiated a Civic Engagement Fund in Bangladesh to support local and national CSOs in achieving Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) 5 and 16. The program, now joined by USAID and Global Affairs Canada (GAC) aims to create a peaceful, just, and inclusive Bangladesh that upholds human rights, good governance, and gender equality. By pooling funds and promoting coordination, this multi-donor programme will reduce costs, expand reach, and foster holistic support for the CSO sector. It will also establish a mechanism for dialogue among the Government of Bangladesh, donors, and CSOs to advance SDGs 5 and 16. The EU aims at contributing indirectly to the activities of the above mentioned Civic Engagement Fund.</narrative>
  </description>
